n the house at least  completely along  partisan lines very clearly now you have  five  republican representatives who say that  they will  vote to impeach but it was as you said a  spirited  debate about the motion to invoke the  25th  amendment largely along partisan lines  this is what some of the representatives  had to say  mr speaker this is a sad day for our  country that we have to come  to the floor in a way to defend  the constitution of the united states at  this time  the facts are very clear the president  called for this seditious attack  while section 4 of the 25th amendment  has never been used  a plain reading of the text coupled with  the context of its ratification  contemplates a very different scenario  from the one we are currently in  let's unite against donald trump who  inspired terrorists to carry a  confederate flag  into this capital display a noose and  desecrate the people's house  the vice president has given you your  answer  before you ask the question no  legitimate purpose to this resolution  remains your ultimatum does violence  to a core feature of the architecture of  the constitution  the devastating bruises on our nation's  soul  can only begin to heal by removing  the weapon used to blunt in us  the vice president must invoke the 25th  amendment  to immediately remove power  from this dangerous president this is a  deeply  unpopular impeachment the public wishes  we were here dealing with  coronavirus not the virus of trump  hatred that you seem to have found  no vaccine for well first we look  forward to  mike really you know now we're talking  about articles of impeachment to be  discussed or debated and voted on in the  house but also it's not going to be a  smooth ride for the president  in the senate senior uh republican  uh leaders there including mitch  mcconnell alluding to the fact that you  know impeachment is quite possible  well what we've seen in the house of  representatives for example  is a recommendation by t